From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Igor Pecovnik <igor@armbian.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 11:15:08 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 40/41] net: pcs: mtk-lynxi: return NULL from
 mtk_pcs_lynxi_create() on failure

mtk_pcs_lynxi_init() now returns ERR_PTR() on failure, and
mtk_pcs_lynxi_create() passes it through. The callers test for NULL
and store the error pointer as a valid PCS. Return NULL on failure, as
before.

Signed-off-by: Igor Pecovnik <igor@armbian.com>
---
 drivers/net/pcs/pcs-mtk-lynxi.c | 6 +++++-
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/pcs/pcs-mtk-lynxi.c b/drivers/net/pcs/pcs-mtk-lynxi.c
index 049e9f0afe63..4df1c19f40d8 100644
--- a/drivers/net/pcs/pcs-mtk-lynxi.c
+++ b/drivers/net/pcs/pcs-mtk-lynxi.c
@@ -393,7 +393,11 @@ struct phylink_pcs *mtk_pcs_lynxi_create(struct device *dev,
 					 struct regmap *regmap, u32 ana_rgc3,
 					 u32 flags)
 {
-	return mtk_pcs_lynxi_init(dev, regmap, ana_rgc3, flags, NULL);
+	struct phylink_pcs *pcs;
+
+	/* Callers expect NULL on failure */
+	pcs = mtk_pcs_lynxi_init(dev, regmap, ana_rgc3, flags, NULL);
+	return IS_ERR(pcs) ? NULL : pcs;
 }
 EXPORT_SYMBOL(mtk_pcs_lynxi_create);
 
